{title: Twinkle, Twinkle, Little Star}
{artist: Jane Taylor}
{genre: folk}
{tempo: 100}
# The Star, Rhymes for the Nursery (1806), first stanza.
# Traditional French tune; original simplified chord accompaniment for MusicMaestro.
{c:Verse}
[C]Twinkle, twinkle, [F]little [C]star,
[F]How I [C]wonder [G]what you [C]are!
[C]Up [F]above the [C]world so [G]high,
[C]Like a [F]diamond [C]in the [G]sky.
[C]Twinkle, twinkle, [F]little [C]star,
[F]How I [C]wonder [G]what you [C]are!
